{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>The father of such as dwell in tents and breed cattle.</b> He was the first of herdsmen in the wilderness, dwelling in tents — a month here and a month there for his flock's pasture. And when the pasture is exhausted in one place, he goes and pitches his tent in another. And its midrash: he built temples for idolatry, as you say: ״סֵמֶל הַקִּנְאָה הַמַּקְנֶה״ (Ezekiel 8) — and likewise ״his brother, the handler of lyre and pipe״ — to sing for idolatry."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:34.604179756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}